      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00066",
          "explanation": "Doctor proactively suggests letting the family ask the patient privately using yes/no questions, addressing the privacy barrier that the elderly person won't openly discuss urinary symptoms.",
          "quote": "问疼不疼还是说不清"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00087",
          "explanation": "Doctor recommends a structured, closed-question approach for the family to use with the patient, specifically to overcome embarrassment about urinary symptoms.",
          "quote": "您列的那四句问药师/门诊的话，已经基本抓住了要点"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO2 (discover hidden urinary symptoms due to embarrassment) was triggered when the family reported the patient couldn't/wouldn't articulate pain. The doctor responded by instructing the family to use closed-ended questions and to ask privately, and later reinforced this with a symptom checklist. This actively overcame the privacy barrier and enabled accurate symptom assessment.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00066",
          "explanation": "Doctor instructs family to photograph or read aloud the key report pages (title, drug sensitivity table, renal function) to compensate for fragmented, illegible screenshots.",
          "quote": "把报告每一行都拍照或念给我听"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00152",
          "explanation": "Doctor further refines the navigation plan: take all drug boxes to pharmacy, get a printed list, and ask specific questions about renal function and drug interactions.",
          "quote": "把所有药盒都带去"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO3 (navigate fragmented external reports and make plan executable) was triggered by the family's admission that they had only partial screenshots and were unsure of which reports were current. The doctor provided a concrete, step-by-step plan to capture the relevant report sections, organize drug boxes, and contact the ordering department, making the plan executable despite the information gap.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00125",
          "explanation": "Family reveals they have already started self-purchased antibiotics. Doctor immediately repairs by checking the drug name, dosage, and clarifying that it was a prescription, not self-medication.",
          "quote": "我们也没有自己买抗生素"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00199",
          "explanation": "Doctor confirms the antibiotic from the pharmacy, checks the dose, and integrates it with the existing anticoagulant/antiplatelet regimen, repairing the potential self-medication risk.",
          "quote": "头孢克肟胶囊，规格我看是 100mg/粒"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO4 (repair external self-medication attempt) was triggered when the family mentioned they had already obtained an antibiotic. The doctor immediately asked for the drug name, dosage, and whether it was a prescription, then verified that it was a clinical decision and not self-bought, and integrated it safely into the plan alongside rivaroxaban/clopidogrel. This repaired a potential handoff gap and prevented self-medication error.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    }
